hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3003","**
Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ma'mar ibn Rib'iyy, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani, who informed us Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to 'Ata': ""I heard Ibn 'Abbas say: 'You were only commanded to perform Tawaf, and you were not commanded to enter it.'""

He said: ""There was no prohibition against entering it, but I heard him say: 'Usamah ibn Zayd informed me that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) when he entered the House, he supplicated in all its corners.'""

I said: ""Its corners—its four corners?""

He said: ""Rather, in every direction of the House.""

---"
